index 57803ed..f215c59 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -3,29 +3,76 @@
 A small task tracker: a JSON API over SQLite and a one-page interface. No dependencies: Node.js 22.18 or later runs
 the TypeScript sources directly and brings SQLite (`node:sqlite`).
 
 ```sh
 npm start        # http://localhost:3000, data in tasks.db (PORT and DB_PATH change them)
-npm test         # the API tests (node:test)
+npm test         # the API tests (node:test), accounts included
 ```
 
 ## API
 
 Every body is JSON. A task is `{ "id": 1, "title": "Buy milk", "done": false, "created_at": "2026-01-31T09:00:00.000Z" }`.
 
 | Method and path | What it does | Answers |
 |---|---|---|
-| `GET /api/tasks` | Lists the tasks, oldest first; `?done=true` or `?done=false` keeps the done or the open ones | 200, an array of tasks |
+| `POST /api/users` | Creates an account from `{ "username", "password" }` | 201 `{ "id": 1, "username": "alice" }`, 400 `{ "error": "invalid username" }`, 400 `{ "error": "password too short" }`, or 409 `{ "error": "username taken" }` |
+| `POST /api/sessions` | Signs in with `{ "username", "password" }` | 201 `{ "token": "…" }`, or 401 `{ "error": "invalid credentials" }` |
+| `DELETE /api/sessions` | Signs out: the token in the `Authorization` header stops working | 204, or 401 `{ "error": "authentication required" }` |
+| `GET /api/tasks` | Lists your tasks, oldest first; `?done=true` or `?done=false` keeps the done or the open ones | 200, an array of tasks |
 | `POST /api/tasks` | Creates a task from `{ "title": "…" }` | 201, the task |
 | `GET /api/tasks/:id` | Reads a task | 200, or 404 `{ "error": "task not found" }` |
 | `PATCH /api/tasks/:id` | Changes `title` and / or `done` | 200, the task, or 404 |
 | `DELETE /api/tasks/:id` | Deletes a task | 204, or 404 |
 
-Errors answer `{ "error": "<message>" }`.
+Errors answer `{ "error": "<message>" }`. A body that is not valid JSON answers 400 `{ "error": "invalid JSON" }`.
+
+## Accounts and authentication
+
+Each user has an account and sees only their own tasks.
+
+- A username is lowercased first (it is stored and compared in lowercase), then it must be 3 to 32 characters among `a-z`, `0-9` and `_`; otherwise 400 `invalid username`. A username already taken, in any case, answers 409 `username taken`.
+- A password has at least 10 characters; otherwise 400 `password too short`.
+- Signing in with a wrong username or a wrong password gives the same answer: 401 `invalid credentials`.
+- Every `/api/tasks` route needs the header `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. A missing, malformed or unknown token answers 401 `{ "error": "authentication required" }`. The page and its files stay public.
+- A task belongs to the user who created it. Reading, changing or deleting another user's task answers 404 `{ "error": "task not found" }`, exactly as for a task that does not exist.
+
+The page has a sign-up and a sign-in form, sends the token with every request, and has a sign-out button.
+
+### Example
+
+```sh
+BASE=http://localhost:3000
+
+# Sign up (answers 201 with the id and the username)
+curl -sS --fail-with-body "$BASE/api/users" \
+  --json '{"username": "alice", "password": "a long enough password"}'
+
+# Sign in, and keep the token in a shell variable
+TOKEN=$(curl -sS --fail-with-body "$BASE/api/sessions" \
+  --json '{"username": "alice", "password": "a long enough password"}' | jq -er .token)
+
+# Use the token
+curl -sS --fail-with-body "$BASE/api/tasks" --json '{"title": "Buy milk"}' \
+  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN"
+curl -sS --fail-with-body "$BASE/api/tasks" -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN"
+
+# Sign out (204): the token no longer works
+curl -sS --fail-with-body -X DELETE "$BASE/api/sessions" -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN"
+```
+
+### Security notes
+
+- Passwords are salted (a random salt per user) and hashed with scrypt (`node:crypto`), and compared in constant time.
+- A token is 32 random bytes from the operating system's random source. Only its SHA-256 hash is stored.
+- No response contains a password or a hash.
+- Tokens do not expire: only signing out revokes one.
+- There is no rate limiting and no password change or reset yet.
+- Tasks created before accounts existed stay in the database (with no owner, `user_id` NULL), but no user sees them.
 
 ## Layout
 
 - `src/db.ts`: opens the database and runs the migrations (`PRAGMA user_version` counts those applied).
-- `src/tasks.ts`: the queries.
+- `src/users.ts`: the accounts and the sessions (passwords, tokens, sign-in).
+- `src/tasks.ts`: the queries, each scoped to the user.
 - `src/app.ts`: the HTTP server and its routes.
-- `public/`: the page.
-- `test/`: the API tests, against a server on a random port with an in-memory database.
+- `public/`: the page, with the sign-up and sign-in forms.
+- `test/`: the API tests (accounts, sessions, and each user seeing only their own tasks), against a server on a random port with an in-memory database.
